That is true.  But at this moment, I don't think there is a lack of 
variety in the end game.  Even now you have to make judicious choices. 
A monk cannot (rather: should not) wear body armor, a barbarian is not 
good at spells, a spell caster has restricted armor choices. I find the 
game is mature enough by now (both NH and Slash'em are) that the end 
games are not quite the same for all classes.  Slash'em is even better 
at this: due to the fact that drain resistance is another desirable 
intrinsic and that pools of water can be created by high spell casters 
below the character's feet (absolutely deadly in a crowd...) one has to 
choose either between the amulet of reflection or the amulet of drain 
resistance or the amulet of flying, one has to choose between gray, deep 
or silver dragon scale mail, between gauntlets of dexterity or gauntlets 
of swimming and speed boots or water walking boots.  A monk cannot have 
all the four desirables: safety from pools (gauntlets of swimming, water 
walking boots or amulet of flying), reflection (permanently only by 
amulet, since the armour is not available), magic resistance (only the 
cloak as safe method) and level drain resistance (only the amulet for 
the monk).  I would usually forgo the last one, which is a necessity 
only in a few places (in the end game, four or five lost levels don't 
matter that much).  Other characters can have all four, but the 
combination to achieve them will depend on game history.


